This code defines a `Packet` structure and a function to populate an array of such structures with unique IP addresses, ports, protocol types, and randomly assigned TCP flags. It supports dynamically specified numbers of packets while ensuring unique port assignments within the valid range (1024-65535). The `generate_unique_port` ensures no port duplication by checking against previously used ports, adjusting for any issues that arise due to limited availability in the port range. Efficient memory management is achieved through a single allocation and deallocation call for the entire packet array. Documentation is provided at the end on how to extend this functionality to support additional protocols.']

